. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * here, we regress the index of gender attitudes on an interaction be
> tween having daughters and 
.         * the respondent being male in addition to the two separate variables
>  and controls. We do so in an 
.         * OLS regression, given that the data are only available for one cros
> s-section. A positive value of the 
.         * interaction term suggests that men more strongly develop pro-equali
> ty gender attitudes than women
.         * when having daughters.
. 
.         reg gender_attitude male_x_num_daughters num_daughters male age age2 
> i.num_children if num_children > 0, vce(robust)

